url: "https://github.com/nickgou-nuke/info-geometry-lean"
abstract: >
  Lean 4 formalization project for information geometry with a maintained
  representation-depth theorem spine
  (count/projective/operator/krein/transport/thermo). Repository-wide lexical
  and declaration-level indexing across Lean sources and black-book chapters
  identifies a stable core centered on modular and spectral operator theory,
  Krein-Clifford doubled geometry, transport/thermodynamic inference lanes
  (including KMS and Bogoliubov structures), and Drazin/inverse-kernel anomaly
  analysis with Einstein-source bridges. The workflow couples hypothesis-first
  black-book research with theorem-target promotion under Lean-native
  architecture audits, DAG diagnostics, and vacuity checks.
